1
00:00:00,410 --> 00:00:01,770
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,770 --> 00:00:03,310
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:05,880 --> 00:00:08,710
What's the point of living
in a palace like this?

4
00:00:09,910 --> 00:00:12,050
What good is having
a mountain of wealth?

5
00:00:12,820 --> 00:00:16,250
When you pass away,
you can't take it with you.

6
00:00:19,860 --> 00:00:21,790
The burden on Madam's heart...

7
00:00:22,530 --> 00:00:24,000
must be so heavy.

8
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:28,270
They're so beautiful.

9
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:32,270
No wonder this family's
eldest grandson is so handsome.

10
00:00:32,370 --> 00:00:33,410
Mrs. Anseong.

11
00:00:34,770 --> 00:00:36,140
(Episode 10)

12
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:38,580
Madam.

13
00:00:42,350 --> 00:00:44,350
I'm so sorry...

14
00:00:44,520 --> 00:00:47,620
Do you even know what sorry means?

15
00:00:50,320 --> 00:00:53,660
I was wrong. Please forgive me.

16
00:00:54,230 --> 00:00:55,360
Have a seat.

17
00:00:55,960 --> 00:00:59,900
You need a good scolding from me.

18
00:01:14,110 --> 00:01:15,180
I...

19
00:01:16,280 --> 00:01:19,350
asked if you knew
what it means to be sorry.

20
00:01:20,690 --> 00:01:21,690
Well?

21
00:01:21,950 --> 00:01:24,960
But tell me,
why are you kneeling in front of me?

22
00:01:25,620 --> 00:01:28,230
Can you answer that for me?

23
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:33,530
I'm just truly sorry, Madam.

24
00:01:34,700 --> 00:01:36,730
I forgot my place.

25
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:38,840
I forgot my place
and came into your room,

26
00:01:40,610 --> 00:01:41,770
speaking so carelessly...

27
00:01:42,270 --> 00:01:45,580
Forgetting your place is a mistake,

28
00:01:45,910 --> 00:01:48,750
but it is not exactly a sin.

29
00:01:50,580 --> 00:01:52,880
It is a mistake anyone could make,

30
00:01:52,920 --> 00:01:54,220
as long as they are human.

31
00:01:54,650 --> 00:01:55,650
Madam.

32
00:01:56,620 --> 00:01:58,160
In my family,

33
00:01:58,620 --> 00:02:02,790
there is more than one person
living with the weight of real sins.

34
00:02:04,900 --> 00:02:06,830
Unfortunately, at least,

35
00:02:07,930 --> 00:02:09,270
that is how my family is.

36
00:02:11,070 --> 00:02:12,070
It is shameful.

37
00:02:13,270 --> 00:02:14,640
Please do not say that.

38
00:02:16,010 --> 00:02:17,010
I...

39
00:02:17,110 --> 00:02:18,610
respect you, Madam.

40
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:20,710
And I always will.

41
00:02:22,850 --> 00:02:24,280
Mrs. Anseong.

42
00:02:25,150 --> 00:02:27,590
- Yes.
- Go to the kitchen...

43
00:02:27,750 --> 00:02:30,520
and quietly bring me a trash can.

44
00:02:31,760 --> 00:02:36,230
I have always thought highly
of your character, Mrs. Anseong.

45
00:02:37,230 --> 00:02:39,200
But while you are in my house,

46
00:02:39,900 --> 00:02:42,670
I would prefer it
if you kept your mouth shut.

47
00:02:43,170 --> 00:02:45,500
However, for my sake,

48
00:02:46,140 --> 00:02:48,110
I hope you keep your ears wide open.

49
00:02:49,410 --> 00:02:50,580
Yes, Madam.

50
00:02:51,080 --> 00:02:53,340
- I will keep that in mind.
- Good.

51
00:02:53,510 --> 00:02:57,080
- I will go bring the tea.
- Okay.

52
00:03:07,190 --> 00:03:08,190
My goodness.

53
00:03:09,130 --> 00:03:11,360
She certainly has a good eye.

54
00:03:11,700 --> 00:03:14,570
Of course he is handsome.

55
00:03:15,630 --> 00:03:18,700
He gets it all from his parents.

56
00:03:19,640 --> 00:03:22,540
You cannot hide your bloodline.

57
00:03:24,340 --> 00:03:27,380
- Gosh, I ate too much.
- Mrs. Anseong.

58
00:03:28,580 --> 00:03:29,610
Yes, ma'am.

59
00:03:29,910 --> 00:03:32,920
Did Mother say anything?

60
00:03:35,020 --> 00:03:36,850
Well, no.

61
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:40,160
She only told me to bring the tea.

62
00:03:41,260 --> 00:03:42,790
Oh, I see.

63
00:03:43,330 --> 00:03:46,700
Mrs. Anseong, dinner tonight
was especially delicious.

64
00:03:46,930 --> 00:03:50,030
- Thank you for your hard work.
- You are too kind, sir.

65
00:03:55,910 --> 00:03:59,110
Oh, the kids must be excited...

66
00:03:59,240 --> 00:04:01,050
to all be together after so long.

67
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:04,020
Did they say
they were drinking earlier?

68
00:04:04,380 --> 00:04:08,850
- I should bring them some snacks.
- Mrs. Anseong is here.

69
00:04:09,050 --> 00:04:11,960
- Let us just go in and rest, okay?
- Oh, honey.

70
00:04:12,320 --> 00:04:15,130
I want to make sure
Seung Yun's bed is comfortable.

71
00:04:15,590 --> 00:04:18,800
How old is Seung Yun
that you need to check his bed?

72
00:04:19,130 --> 00:04:20,370
Let us rest, okay?

73
00:04:20,500 --> 00:04:22,800
- Let us rest. Let us go in.
- But...

74
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:24,200
- I will massage your shoulders.
- Honey...

75
00:04:26,100 --> 00:04:27,110
Underwear?

76
00:04:28,110 --> 00:04:29,110
Is it funny?

77
00:04:29,640 --> 00:04:31,280
Sure, laugh all you want.

78
00:04:31,780 --> 00:04:32,810
I will not charge you for it.

79
00:04:33,780 --> 00:04:37,180
Hey, Do Yun. You should be glad...

80
00:04:37,250 --> 00:04:40,280
that department store employee
did not call security, okay?

81
00:04:40,350 --> 00:04:42,420
If it were me, I would have
called the police right away.

82
00:04:42,790 --> 00:04:45,320
No, she might even
sue you for damages...

83
00:04:45,390 --> 00:04:50,260
for the emotional distress.
Can you imagine how shocked she was?

84
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:52,830
Seung Yun,
do you know what is even funnier?

85
00:04:53,530 --> 00:04:55,100
After doing something like that,

86
00:04:55,170 --> 00:04:58,140
he completely fell
for that department store employee.

87
00:04:58,770 --> 00:05:00,740
What do you keep talking about?

88
00:05:02,970 --> 00:05:04,040
I told you it is not true.

89
00:05:05,180 --> 00:05:07,050
- It is not true.
- It is.

90
00:05:07,350 --> 00:05:08,910
You can never fool my eyes.

91
00:05:10,820 --> 00:05:13,650
Hey, it is very problematic
to fall for someone...

92
00:05:13,720 --> 00:05:15,890
after acting like a pervert.

93
00:05:16,550 --> 00:05:19,220
That is what I am saying.
Anyway, if the situation...

94
00:05:19,290 --> 00:05:21,330
was somewhat resolved,
should that not be the end of it?

95
00:05:21,730 --> 00:05:25,930
But he agonized over it
all by himself for days,

96
00:05:26,430 --> 00:05:28,770
saying he felt so wronged
and uncomfortable...

97
00:05:28,930 --> 00:05:30,130
that he could not take it anymore.

98
00:05:30,130 --> 00:05:31,940
He used that as an excuse
to take me...

99
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:33,270
and have a three-way
confrontation today.

100
00:05:33,810 --> 00:05:36,470
Hey, why did you even bother
going back there?

101
00:05:36,540 --> 00:05:37,880
She must have been
even more shocked.

102
00:05:39,640 --> 00:05:40,850
I did not fall for her.

103
00:05:41,150 --> 00:05:42,310
I would rather die
than be misunderstood...

104
00:05:42,380 --> 00:05:44,380
as a pervert by that woman,
so what was I supposed to do?

105
00:05:44,750 --> 00:05:47,050
I am a team leader
at Hwanggeum Apparel.

106
00:05:47,120 --> 00:05:48,150
And the CEO's son.

107
00:05:48,850 --> 00:05:49,950
Image management is important.

108
00:05:50,420 --> 00:05:51,560
Seung Yun, did you hear that?

109
00:05:51,690 --> 00:05:53,490
Did you hear what Do Yun just said?

110
00:05:54,890 --> 00:05:56,590
Oh, he is interested in her.

111
00:05:56,660 --> 00:05:58,900
He is interested,
so he hates being misunderstood,

112
00:05:58,960 --> 00:06:01,270
and he had to
explain himself somehow.

113
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:03,330
Managing his image
is just an excuse.

114
00:06:03,970 --> 00:06:06,300
So when you went to confront them,
what did the store employee say?

115
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:08,940
She was shocked,
saying she had forgotten about it.

116
00:06:09,610 --> 00:06:11,480
She played it cool
and said it was fine.

117
00:06:12,510 --> 00:06:14,710
She does not care at all,

118
00:06:14,780 --> 00:06:17,450
but he is making a big deal
out of it all by himself.

119
00:06:18,820 --> 00:06:19,820
Then again.

120
00:06:20,550 --> 00:06:24,820
I guess unrequited love
usually starts like that.

121
00:06:26,990 --> 00:06:28,430
I am canceling your credit card
right now.

122
00:06:28,490 --> 00:06:31,060
Come on, why are you being
like this, Do Yun?

123
00:06:31,700 --> 00:06:33,530
Team Leader Cha, sorry.

124
00:06:34,930 --> 00:06:36,000
Oh, I am done teasing you.

125
00:06:37,970 --> 00:06:39,340
I am sleepy. I should go to bed now.

126
00:06:40,840 --> 00:06:42,010
- Good night.
- Go get some rest.

127
00:06:42,070 --> 00:06:43,070
Bye.

128
00:06:45,610 --> 00:06:46,640
Hey, Do Yun.

129
00:06:47,150 --> 00:06:48,980
Hey, you said you prepared
something special,

130
00:06:49,050 --> 00:06:50,680
and it is just beer?

131
00:06:50,750 --> 00:06:53,020
I thought it would be
whiskey or wine, at the very least.

132
00:06:53,180 --> 00:06:55,050
Seung Yun, you drank enough
of that in the US.

133
00:06:55,290 --> 00:06:58,660
Next time, it'll be soju.
Just us guys, without Se Na.

134
00:06:59,620 --> 00:07:00,630
Why?

135
00:07:00,890 --> 00:07:03,360
- Why are you leaving me out?
- Then should I take your card away?

136
00:07:04,660 --> 00:07:06,560
I have never tried soju.

137
00:07:07,130 --> 00:07:08,530
Actually, I cannot drink it.

138
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:12,040
Then you two have a good time.

139
00:07:15,610 --> 00:07:16,610
Cheers.

140
00:07:28,620 --> 00:07:30,120
Madam, what are you looking for?

141
00:07:30,190 --> 00:07:31,360
I will do it.

142
00:07:31,420 --> 00:07:34,060
- Please tell me.
- Oh, stay still.

143
00:07:40,800 --> 00:07:42,900
Premium Galbi Sujak?

144
00:07:46,070 --> 00:07:49,240
You played a nice little trick.

145
00:07:49,970 --> 00:07:51,610
I am sorry, Madam.

146
00:07:52,710 --> 00:07:55,110
What? Are you saying...

147
00:07:55,880 --> 00:07:59,950
that you knew CEO Jeon
was doing this?

148
00:08:00,520 --> 00:08:01,520
Yes.

149
00:08:01,620 --> 00:08:03,590
Since this old woman
is losing her mind,

150
00:08:03,920 --> 00:08:06,320
CEO Jeon must have told you
that if you listen to her,

151
00:08:06,490 --> 00:08:09,960
she would make sure
you are well compensated, right?

152
00:08:12,160 --> 00:08:15,130
Even though I may lose my mind
from time to time...

153
00:08:15,270 --> 00:08:16,270
Mrs. Anseong.

154
00:08:16,770 --> 00:08:18,540
I am the master of this house.

155
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:21,370
I know, Madam.

156
00:08:22,210 --> 00:08:23,880
Act accordingly.

157
00:08:47,230 --> 00:08:48,230
Mom!

158
00:08:49,270 --> 00:08:50,270
Mom!

159
00:08:54,370 --> 00:08:55,470
Mom!

160
00:08:56,240 --> 00:08:57,640
You have to come back soon.

161
00:08:58,140 --> 00:08:59,210
Mom.

162
00:08:59,980 --> 00:09:01,110
Mom!

163
00:09:03,310 --> 00:09:04,420
Mom!

164
00:09:05,780 --> 00:09:07,250
You will come back soon, right?

165
00:09:07,920 --> 00:09:09,450
You have to come back soon.

166
00:09:10,420 --> 00:09:11,590
Mom.

167
00:09:12,490 --> 00:09:13,760
Mom.

168
00:09:17,130 --> 00:09:18,660
Mom.

169
00:09:21,530 --> 00:09:22,730
Mom.

170
00:09:24,470 --> 00:09:26,340
You have to come back soon.

171
00:09:38,620 --> 00:09:40,890
I have put everything behind,
so why again?

172
00:09:41,650 --> 00:09:43,250
What did you put behind you, honey?

173
00:09:45,420 --> 00:09:46,420
It is nothing.

174
00:09:47,730 --> 00:09:48,930
I must have had a nightmare.

175
00:09:51,230 --> 00:09:52,330
You are up early.

176
00:09:52,760 --> 00:09:53,760
Yes.

177
00:09:53,970 --> 00:09:56,630
I think Mother might call for me
before breakfast.

178
00:09:58,340 --> 00:10:00,710
I submitted
our company operations report yesterday.

179
00:10:01,110 --> 00:10:04,280
It looked like she was reviewing it
very thoroughly on her laptop.

180
00:10:04,710 --> 00:10:06,110
Are you still afraid
of being scolded by Mother...

181
00:10:06,440 --> 00:10:08,450
at your age?

182
00:10:09,280 --> 00:10:11,520
Well, it is not that I am afraid.

183
00:10:12,120 --> 00:10:14,850
She is just intimidating
when it comes to work.

184
00:10:15,350 --> 00:10:20,120
For the sake of her health,
I wish she would just trust us...

185
00:10:20,590 --> 00:10:23,290
and leave the management to us now.

186
00:10:24,300 --> 00:10:27,030
You should bring it up
to her this time.

187
00:10:27,870 --> 00:10:30,130
Yes, I was thinking the same thing.

188
00:10:31,270 --> 00:10:33,440
I will find a good time to tell her.

189
00:10:34,440 --> 00:10:36,010
I will go make some coffee.

190
00:10:49,650 --> 00:10:51,520
What is this?

191
00:10:51,960 --> 00:10:54,960
Even the tables we only use for
holiday memorial services are out.

192
00:10:57,400 --> 00:10:58,730
Mrs. Choi.

193
00:10:59,460 --> 00:11:00,560
Are you praying?

194
00:11:01,500 --> 00:11:02,870
Are you chanting a Buddhist prayer?

195
00:11:03,570 --> 00:11:05,940
We are hungry.

196
00:11:09,570 --> 00:11:13,840
- Sweetie, go ahead and eat, okay?
- Okay.

197
00:11:13,940 --> 00:11:16,480
But Mom said I can only eat...

198
00:11:16,550 --> 00:11:18,750
after you take your first bite.

199
00:11:33,730 --> 00:11:34,730
Da Mi.

200
00:11:35,470 --> 00:11:36,470
Yes, Grandma.

201
00:11:36,570 --> 00:11:38,900
You need to get off work
a little early today.

202
00:11:41,040 --> 00:11:42,540
Why is that, Grandma?

203
00:11:43,010 --> 00:11:44,080
Will that be difficult?

204
00:11:44,780 --> 00:11:46,180
No, I will come home early.

205
00:11:47,710 --> 00:11:50,410
Close the restaurant
two hours early as well, Mi Mi.

206
00:11:51,520 --> 00:11:52,580
What?

207
00:11:53,050 --> 00:11:55,390
Mom, is it
Grandpa's memorial service?

208
00:11:56,120 --> 00:11:57,460
Is it not still a ways off?

209
00:11:57,790 --> 00:11:58,960
Mrs. Choi,

210
00:11:59,760 --> 00:12:01,730
what is going on?

211
00:12:02,390 --> 00:12:03,960
You are telling Da Mi
to come home early,

212
00:12:04,030 --> 00:12:05,130
and to close the restaurant early.

213
00:12:06,830 --> 00:12:08,600
Why are you doing this?

214
00:12:09,200 --> 00:12:10,900
Dae Chi is on leave
for the first time in a while...

215
00:12:10,970 --> 00:12:12,400
and staying with us.

216
00:12:13,070 --> 00:12:15,010
So I thought we could all gather
and play yutnori,

217
00:12:15,070 --> 00:12:16,140
just the family.

218
00:12:20,310 --> 00:12:21,550
Well, Mother.

219
00:12:22,650 --> 00:12:26,880
I will just talk to you
about this matter separately.

220
00:12:28,220 --> 00:12:29,320
I was wrong.

221
00:12:30,190 --> 00:12:32,390
Please just eat
your breakfast first.

222
00:12:34,930 --> 00:12:39,000
I just want to play yutnori,
so why are there so many complaints?

223
00:12:39,930 --> 00:12:42,100
Da Mi, come home early,

224
00:12:42,170 --> 00:12:44,770
draw a new game board on a calendar,
and set it up.

225
00:12:45,270 --> 00:12:46,440
Do you understand?

226
00:12:46,840 --> 00:12:48,170
Yes, Grandma.

227
00:13:04,520 --> 00:13:05,560
Oh, right.

228
00:13:15,100 --> 00:13:16,330
Why did you come back in?

229
00:13:24,740 --> 00:13:25,780
What is it?

230
00:13:27,410 --> 00:13:29,210
I met Mi Seon yesterday.

231
00:13:30,410 --> 00:13:32,450
She said you were probably
out of face cream...

232
00:13:32,520 --> 00:13:33,580
and told me to give this to you.

233
00:13:33,880 --> 00:13:35,020
You met Mi Seon?

234
00:13:35,890 --> 00:13:37,450
Why are you
just telling me this now?

235
00:13:37,860 --> 00:13:39,690
You were throwing such a fit
at me yesterday.

236
00:13:39,760 --> 00:13:41,560
Did you think I had any time
to tell you?

237
00:13:42,930 --> 00:13:43,960
Where did she say she lives?

238
00:13:44,460 --> 00:13:47,600
How is she making a living?
Did she look okay?

239
00:13:47,670 --> 00:13:48,830
Did she look sick at all?

240
00:13:49,970 --> 00:13:52,870
Never mind.
You know her address, right?

241
00:13:53,200 --> 00:13:54,440
You know it, right?

242
00:13:54,940 --> 00:13:56,070
What if I do?

243
00:13:57,140 --> 00:13:58,910
Text it to me right now.

244
00:13:59,540 --> 00:14:00,540
Got it?

245
00:14:02,310 --> 00:14:03,810
I asked if you got it.

246
00:14:04,950 --> 00:14:06,150
I got it.

247
00:14:07,380 --> 00:14:08,450
But Mi Seon...

248
00:14:08,590 --> 00:14:10,190
probably will not be too happy
to see you, Mom.

249
00:14:10,450 --> 00:14:12,220
Do you think I am going
because I want to see her?

250
00:14:12,890 --> 00:14:14,290
Just send me the address.

251
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:19,430
But Mom,

252
00:14:20,500 --> 00:14:22,430
did Grandma figure everything out?

253
00:14:22,830 --> 00:14:25,640
Is that why she is calling
our whole family together?

254
00:14:31,410 --> 00:14:33,940
Well, I haven't done anything wrong.

255
00:14:34,880 --> 00:14:36,010
I will be on my way.

256
00:14:45,790 --> 00:14:47,060
Do you have everything?

257
00:14:50,290 --> 00:14:51,330
What is going on?

258
00:14:51,400 --> 00:14:53,060
You washed your face
and even shaved this morning.

259
00:14:53,330 --> 00:14:56,270
Hey, did you not
leave for work earlier?

260
00:14:58,440 --> 00:14:59,470
Auntie.

261
00:14:59,600 --> 00:15:02,540
Can I take this book
to daycare to read?

262
00:15:03,040 --> 00:15:04,440
I already read all of mine.

263
00:15:04,880 --> 00:15:08,350
This one? This one
has some pictures...

264
00:15:08,410 --> 00:15:11,050
that are a bit inappropriate
for kids, Su Ah.

265
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:12,280
- What?
- What do you mean?

266
00:15:12,350 --> 00:15:14,050
I just wanted to show my friends...

267
00:15:14,150 --> 00:15:16,420
the pictures of the handsome guy.

268
00:15:16,850 --> 00:15:20,320
Since they are models,
most of them are either unique...

269
00:15:20,390 --> 00:15:22,460
or pretty and handsome.

270
00:15:23,230 --> 00:15:26,700
No,
it says he is a designer, Auntie.

271
00:15:27,500 --> 00:15:29,300
A designer? Who is it?

272
00:15:30,470 --> 00:15:32,140
Right here, this guy.

273
00:15:35,140 --> 00:15:36,210
Wait, this guy...

274
00:15:37,010 --> 00:15:38,840
It is him, Jaden Cha.

275
00:15:39,780 --> 00:15:40,880
Jaden Cha?

276
00:15:41,650 --> 00:15:45,150
Hey, what kind of name is that?
What is he kicking?

277
00:15:45,920 --> 00:15:46,920
Hey, but...

278
00:15:47,480 --> 00:15:48,750
he is pretty good-looking.

279
00:15:49,150 --> 00:15:52,490
Su Ah,
I will buy you a new storybook.

280
00:15:52,790 --> 00:15:54,530
I need to take this one with me.

281
00:15:55,060 --> 00:15:56,130
- I am leaving.
- Okay.

282
00:15:56,130 --> 00:15:58,300
Auntie, you have to buy me
a storybook.

283
00:15:58,730 --> 00:15:59,730
Got it.

284
00:16:05,300 --> 00:16:06,370
(K Department Store)

285
00:16:11,680 --> 00:16:12,880
Oh, my gosh.

286
00:16:13,110 --> 00:16:14,580
How could I not recognize
my own role model...

287
00:16:14,580 --> 00:16:17,410
when he was right in front of me?
And multiple times, at that.

288
00:16:19,550 --> 00:16:22,250
"He plans to return to Korea,"

289
00:16:22,350 --> 00:16:24,390
"and has signed a contract
as the head designer..."

290
00:16:24,460 --> 00:16:25,690
"for Hwanggeum Apparel."

291
00:16:27,990 --> 00:16:29,090
Kang Da Mi...

292
00:16:29,260 --> 00:16:32,200
I should've just given him my number
when he asked for it.

293
00:16:33,500 --> 00:16:37,600
Mom has really good eyesight.
Do I need to get glasses?

294
00:16:40,570 --> 00:16:43,310
But after achieving
such massive success in the US,

295
00:16:43,770 --> 00:16:45,040
why would he
bother coming back here?

296
00:16:45,980 --> 00:16:49,480
Usually, going to Paris or Italy
is the standard route.

297
00:16:50,980 --> 00:16:52,880
- Hey.
- Oh, you startled me.

298
00:16:53,180 --> 00:16:54,720
(K Department Store)

299
00:16:58,360 --> 00:16:59,790
Welcome.

300
00:17:00,060 --> 00:17:01,630
I just came in
without an appointment.

301
00:17:01,630 --> 00:17:02,660
Is that okay?

302
00:17:02,960 --> 00:17:06,530
Yes, that's perfectly fine.
It's great to see you again.

303
00:17:07,200 --> 00:17:10,300
Oh, you don't have to be
so formal with me.

304
00:17:10,370 --> 00:17:13,270
Just relax and be comfortable.
I'm younger than you.

305
00:17:13,800 --> 00:17:15,040
You are a customer.

306
00:17:15,540 --> 00:17:17,940
And I am genuinely happy
to see you again.

307
00:17:18,880 --> 00:17:20,840
When I came
with my brother yesterday,

308
00:17:21,380 --> 00:17:24,050
you must have been
pretty dumbfounded, right?

309
00:17:24,920 --> 00:17:27,020
I will apologize on his behalf.

310
00:17:27,580 --> 00:17:29,790
No, I am really okay.

311
00:17:30,220 --> 00:17:32,990
Is there a specific item
you are looking for?

312
00:17:33,390 --> 00:17:37,330
No. But whatever I like here today,

313
00:17:37,560 --> 00:17:39,900
I am going to
completely sweep it all up.

314
00:17:40,660 --> 00:17:41,700
Excuse me?

315
00:17:50,870 --> 00:17:53,210
My name is Se Na. Cha Se Na.

316
00:17:53,340 --> 00:17:54,410
It is nice to meet you.

317
00:17:55,380 --> 00:17:57,310
The pleasure is all mine.

318
00:18:11,730 --> 00:18:12,730
Yes.

319
00:18:20,800 --> 00:18:21,810
Yes.

320
00:18:36,890 --> 00:18:38,120
I am torn.

321
00:18:39,320 --> 00:18:41,120
Which one do you think looks better?

322
00:18:43,360 --> 00:18:44,800
The one on the left...

323
00:18:44,800 --> 00:18:47,460
would go much better with the outfit
you chose today.

324
00:18:47,900 --> 00:18:48,900
However,

325
00:18:50,430 --> 00:18:53,200
only eight of these were brought
into the country,

326
00:18:53,240 --> 00:18:55,870
and this is the very last one
we have in stock,

327
00:18:56,210 --> 00:18:57,640
so it is quite expensive.

328
00:18:58,410 --> 00:18:59,780
Oh, is that all?

329
00:19:02,250 --> 00:19:04,720
Don't worry. I have BC.

330
00:19:05,380 --> 00:19:07,480
- BC?
- My brother's card.

331
00:19:07,680 --> 00:19:09,190
The brother who came
with me yesterday.

332
00:19:10,390 --> 00:19:11,390
I see.

333
00:19:11,460 --> 00:19:12,990
Then I will try them on one by one.

334
00:19:18,960 --> 00:19:21,800
How can she not have
a single twisted bone in her body?

335
00:19:22,030 --> 00:19:24,400
She must be from a family
with no issues, right?

336
00:19:25,840 --> 00:19:26,870
I am jealous.

337
00:19:27,470 --> 00:19:30,470
My family is way too messed up.

338
00:19:31,580 --> 00:19:33,380
(CEO Jeon Jin Hee)

339
00:19:33,410 --> 00:19:36,380
When I came into work today,
the company seemed quite chaotic.

340
00:19:36,650 --> 00:19:37,650
Right.

341
00:19:37,710 --> 00:19:40,120
The scholarship students
that our company sponsors...

342
00:19:40,180 --> 00:19:42,250
are having
their invitation event today.

343
00:19:42,690 --> 00:19:44,520
Oh, that was today.

344
00:19:45,520 --> 00:19:46,520
By the way,

345
00:19:46,590 --> 00:19:48,990
you know that the new head designer
is arriving, right?

346
00:19:49,290 --> 00:19:50,290
Yes, CEO Jeon.

347
00:19:50,360 --> 00:19:53,100
Our company's new product planning
for the first half of next year...

348
00:19:53,560 --> 00:19:55,300
will change drastically.

349
00:19:55,400 --> 00:19:57,770
Please make preparations
so that we can respond flexibly.

350
00:19:58,840 --> 00:20:00,500
Since this person has only worked
in the US,

351
00:20:00,570 --> 00:20:02,610
the reactions to accepting them
in the company...

352
00:20:03,470 --> 00:20:05,610
will not be
unconditionally favorable.

353
00:20:07,110 --> 00:20:08,880
I understand exactly what you mean.

354
00:20:09,780 --> 00:20:12,050
- You may leave.
- Yes, I will take my leave.

355
00:20:16,320 --> 00:20:18,320
(CEO Jeon Jin Hee)

356
00:20:22,430 --> 00:20:23,590
Mom!

357
00:20:25,030 --> 00:20:28,000
Mom. You will come back soon, right?

358
00:20:28,670 --> 00:20:30,170
You have to come back soon.

359
00:20:31,100 --> 00:20:32,270
Mom!

360
00:20:34,270 --> 00:20:35,470
My only children...

361
00:20:37,370 --> 00:20:40,180
are Do Yun and my daughter, Se Na.

362
00:20:41,650 --> 00:20:43,050
Just the two of them.

363
00:20:45,180 --> 00:20:46,980
It will always be
just the two of them.

364
00:20:50,650 --> 00:20:52,620
(Hwanggeum Apparel)

365
00:20:52,690 --> 00:20:54,660
(CEO Jeon Jin Hee)

366
00:21:04,030 --> 00:21:05,040
Ma'am,

367
00:21:05,100 --> 00:21:07,800
the alterations should be done
in one or two days at the earliest.

368
00:21:07,970 --> 00:21:09,370
Would you like them delivered
to your home?

369
00:21:09,540 --> 00:21:11,140
Yes, please do that.

370
00:21:12,680 --> 00:21:14,540
It is too much
to carry alone, right?

371
00:21:16,010 --> 00:21:17,350
I will process your payment.

372
00:21:17,710 --> 00:21:19,050
I need to give you my card.

373
00:21:21,820 --> 00:21:23,950
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

374
00:21:24,250 --> 00:21:27,120
- Would you like installments...
- No, in full, please.

375
00:21:27,960 --> 00:21:29,030
Yes, ma'am.

376
00:21:32,900 --> 00:21:36,470
Excuse me, ma'am.
You mentioned this is BC,

377
00:21:36,530 --> 00:21:38,540
and since your purchase amount today
is quite large,

378
00:21:38,940 --> 00:21:41,740
may I ask if you have obtained
consent or permission...

379
00:21:41,810 --> 00:21:44,240
from him to use this card?

380
00:21:44,740 --> 00:21:48,010
This is to prepare for any issues
that might arise later.

381
00:21:50,010 --> 00:21:52,880
There is no problem.
I will take responsibility.

382
00:21:52,950 --> 00:21:54,050
I am telling you to trust me.

383
00:21:55,420 --> 00:21:57,650
Then the verbal verification process
is complete,

384
00:21:57,720 --> 00:22:01,320
and I would like to reiterate
that we have also confirmed...

385
00:22:01,430 --> 00:22:02,430
that you'll take
all responsibility...

386
00:22:02,490 --> 00:22:04,030
for anything
that may occur hereafter.

387
00:22:04,360 --> 00:22:05,600
I will process the payment.

388
00:22:13,900 --> 00:22:15,610
(K Department Store)

389
00:22:22,450 --> 00:22:24,950
Right, there has to be a sunny day
once in a while.

390
00:22:25,280 --> 00:22:26,320
Even if it is just at work.

391
00:22:30,890 --> 00:22:32,360
The doors are closing.

392
00:22:34,930 --> 00:22:35,960
Hey, Team Leader Cha.

393
00:22:37,130 --> 00:22:39,530
- The doors are closing.
- Where are you heading?

394
00:22:40,030 --> 00:22:42,600
Oh, yes.
I have some urgent business.

395
00:22:49,070 --> 00:22:52,780
Just how much did she swipe?
That's 4,850 dollars.

396
00:22:53,780 --> 00:22:55,310
It's 6,580 dollars.

397
00:22:55,550 --> 00:22:57,350
(Cha Seung Yun Approved,
18,000 dollars in full)

398
00:22:57,410 --> 00:22:58,450
What, 18,000 dollars?

399
00:23:02,820 --> 00:23:06,790
I heard my mom is downstairs,
so I am heading down for a moment.

400
00:23:07,690 --> 00:23:08,930
Oh, I see.

401
00:23:12,330 --> 00:23:13,900
When you watch things like dramas,

402
00:23:14,100 --> 00:23:17,430
the elevator always
breaks down at times like this.

403
00:23:18,270 --> 00:23:19,300
Break down.

404
00:23:20,370 --> 00:23:23,170
Please break down, elevator. Okay?

405
00:23:25,140 --> 00:23:26,310
Oh, you startled me.

406
00:23:27,140 --> 00:23:29,050
Mom, what are you doing?

407
00:23:29,610 --> 00:23:31,480
Is it not the busiest time
for the restaurant right now?

408
00:23:32,580 --> 00:23:35,020
If you know it is a busy time,
you should go out and help.

409
00:23:35,320 --> 00:23:37,150
I was actually
going to eat some ramyeon...

410
00:23:37,720 --> 00:23:38,890
and head out.

411
00:23:39,890 --> 00:23:43,430
But who are you planning to give
all these side dishes to?

412
00:23:43,960 --> 00:23:45,530
Dae Chi is also home.

413
00:23:46,530 --> 00:23:48,770
She met the wrong man
and ruined her own life,

414
00:23:48,770 --> 00:23:51,370
so I am just going to visit her
and feed her. Why?

415
00:23:53,470 --> 00:23:55,240
No, that is...

416
00:23:57,540 --> 00:23:58,580
But you are my mom.

417
00:24:02,610 --> 00:24:05,620
- Get out. Get out, you brat.
- I did not say anything wrong,

418
00:24:05,620 --> 00:24:07,420
- so why hit me?
- Are you not going to get out?

419
00:24:07,480 --> 00:24:10,190
Gosh, that hurts.
I will leave. I am leaving. Gosh!

420
00:24:14,560 --> 00:24:16,760
He only feels sorry
for his own miserable self.

421
00:24:17,330 --> 00:24:18,960
He is just a pitiful fool.

422
00:24:19,960 --> 00:24:22,170
Such a pain.

423
00:24:25,940 --> 00:24:28,410
Even a pet dog
would not be beaten like this.

424
00:24:29,510 --> 00:24:31,370
It is not like divorce
is a crime these days,

425
00:24:31,580 --> 00:24:32,880
so why is she acting like that?

426
00:24:33,410 --> 00:24:34,440
Gosh, it hurts.

427
00:24:43,050 --> 00:24:44,120
Hey.

428
00:24:45,390 --> 00:24:46,420
Is something wrong?

429
00:24:47,060 --> 00:24:48,060
Why?

430
00:24:48,160 --> 00:24:51,700
Well, it is not like
I am worried about you or anything.

431
00:24:54,100 --> 00:24:55,570
It is just that, other than work,

432
00:24:55,730 --> 00:24:57,130
and the time you spend
eating and sleeping,

433
00:24:57,200 --> 00:24:58,740
you never put a book down,

434
00:24:59,000 --> 00:25:00,500
so this is very unusual for you.

435
00:25:01,140 --> 00:25:02,640
You said you got some time off,

436
00:25:02,710 --> 00:25:03,870
but coming home
and spacing out like this...

437
00:25:03,940 --> 00:25:04,940
is also strange.

438
00:25:07,610 --> 00:25:10,480
- Just worry about yourself.
- Unbelievable.

439
00:25:11,280 --> 00:25:13,220
Are you deaf?

440
00:25:13,650 --> 00:25:16,220
I told you I was not asking
because I was worried.

441
00:25:17,620 --> 00:25:18,660
Goodness.

442
00:25:23,330 --> 00:25:25,930
Hey, what is going on?

443
00:25:27,130 --> 00:25:28,870
What is going on
that makes you sigh...

444
00:25:28,930 --> 00:25:31,640
loud enough to travel from Seoul
all the way to Busan?

445
00:25:33,240 --> 00:25:34,270
Did you by any chance...

446
00:25:35,740 --> 00:25:37,170
get disciplined at work?

447
00:25:38,210 --> 00:25:39,980
Come on, do I look like
the type to do that?

448
00:25:40,280 --> 00:25:41,650
True.

449
00:25:42,180 --> 00:25:44,810
You are the type
to hand out the discipline.

450
00:25:45,020 --> 00:25:46,880
And you would do it
without any mercy.

451
00:25:47,350 --> 00:25:49,050
I should just... Darn it.

452
00:25:51,250 --> 00:25:52,320
Darn it.

453
00:25:59,060 --> 00:26:00,960
To put out this urgent fire
right now,

454
00:26:01,670 --> 00:26:04,500
Mom is the only one.
The only one who can help me.

455
00:26:15,350 --> 00:26:17,910
She is drowning in debt.
What money could she possibly have?

456
00:26:20,720 --> 00:26:22,590
If she signed the divorce papers
and split up,

457
00:26:23,350 --> 00:26:25,120
she should just focus
on living her own life.

458
00:26:28,260 --> 00:26:29,730
Yes, she is too soft-hearted,

459
00:26:31,130 --> 00:26:33,460
which is why she lived
with my foolish son for so long.

460
00:26:36,530 --> 00:26:37,930
How much is this anyway?

461
00:26:39,140 --> 00:26:40,940
She must have paid
at least 50 dollars for it.

462
00:26:44,070 --> 00:26:45,080
Goodness.

463
00:26:47,080 --> 00:26:48,240
Just wait until I see her.

464
00:26:49,180 --> 00:26:50,850
I am going to smack her on the back.

465
00:26:55,150 --> 00:26:56,190
Mom.

466
00:27:01,160 --> 00:27:02,330
Mom, I am coming in.

467
00:27:03,630 --> 00:27:04,690
Why would you come in?

468
00:27:05,360 --> 00:27:07,760
This is my room. Get out.

469
00:27:09,170 --> 00:27:10,500
What is wrong, Mom?

470
00:27:11,630 --> 00:27:12,640
Mom.

471
00:27:13,040 --> 00:27:14,840
Enough with calling me Mom.

472
00:27:16,870 --> 00:27:19,540
Stop calling me that, you brats.

473
00:27:32,520 --> 00:27:35,330
(Mission: Mompossible)

474
00:27:35,530 --> 00:27:37,460
- Hello, Chairwoman.
- Hello, Chairwoman.

475
00:27:37,530 --> 00:27:41,930
Am I some kind of mob boss?
Who told you to do this nonsense?

476
00:27:43,030 --> 00:27:45,540
Why do you have my things?

477
00:27:45,600 --> 00:27:46,670
Where did you get them?

478
00:27:47,200 --> 00:27:48,540
Why are you speaking
to me like that?

479
00:27:48,610 --> 00:27:50,540
As if I stole them or something.

480
00:27:51,470 --> 00:27:54,740
I spoiled you, and you turned
into a brat in an instant.

481
00:27:54,810 --> 00:27:55,810
Mom.

482
00:27:56,710 --> 00:27:58,110
What is so great about money anyway?

483
00:28:01,020 --> 00:28:03,550
(Mission: Mompossible)
